{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"rancid-aerophobic-skylark","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context and confirmed defect\\n\\nMerged main at d2dea317ec fails every Gerrit Verified matrix cell before pytest:  is 808 LOC against the locked 800-LOC cap. Change 1730 reproduced the same failure on Ubuntu Python 3.11/3.12/3.13 and macOS Python 3.13 in run 31726058931. The importer patch never executed. This is distinct from deferred repo-wide sweep cinderlike-lucky-akitainu: it is the narrow main-is-red regression blocking all changes.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\nTwo individually reviewed config additions accumulated through Gerrit's server-side main history without preserving module-size headroom. The monolithic  coercion registry remains colocated with dataclasses despite already being an import-independent table over  helpers, leaving the schema module above its enforced hard cap.\\n\\n## Plan\\n\\n- Extract the complete  registry, unchanged, to a new  leaf that imports only the coercion helpers it calls.\\n- Import  back into ; preserve every key, coercer, validation bound, and public behavior.\\n- Prove structural equivalence with the config tests and full lint/typecheck gates; seed a mutation that removes one registry entry and confirm existing config-surface coverage catches it.\\n- Do not raise or alter the 800-LOC limit and do not broaden into the deferred repo-wide sweep.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ]  is below 800 LOC and the new module is at least 100 LOC, following the existing registry seam.\\n- [ ] Every  section/key and coercer is preserved exactly; config-surface and focused config tests pass.\\n- [ ] The module-size gate, lint, and typecheck pass.\\n- [ ] A defect-seeded missing-registry-entry mutation is observed RED, then the final implementation is restored GREEN.\\n\\n## File impact\\n\\n- src/rebar/_config_schema.py\\n- src/rebar/_config_sections.py\\n","id":"9843-170c-4d9e-446b","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["ci","module-size","regression"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Restore main CI after _config_schema.py exceeded the locked module-size cap"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786643335315066001,"uuid":"fdb53b86-ad25-49b7-8d04-2b18fb505712"}